  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT PRESENTATION",
      "text": "Patient Jennifer Garcia was triaged in the emergency department following acute onset of lightheadedness and palpitations earlier this morning. Initial hemodynamic parameters were reviewed and patient was placed on telemetry."
    },
    {
      "title": "HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS",
      "text": "The patient describes experiencing recurrent lightheadedness over the preceding 48 hours without syncope. Initial emergency workup revealed that initial bun was measured at 13.6 mg/dL. Point-of-care laboratory screening additionally noted alanine aminotransferase (alt) resulted at 27.6 U/L. Given these findings, the patient was transitioned to the Clinical Decision Unit for 24-hour observation."
    },
    {
      "title": "OBSERVATION UNIT CLINICAL COURSE",
      "text": "Throughout the observation unit stay, continuous telemetry showed normal sinus rhythm without pause or tachyarrhythmia. The patient was administered Amlodipine at a dose of 2.5 mg orally once daily, which promptly alleviated acute symptoms. Follow-up protocol monitoring of sodium demonstrated 149.8 mmol/L (HIGH). Orthostatic blood pressures were negative upon ambulation."
    },
    {
      "title": "DISCHARGE REGIMEN",
      "text": "Patient was deemed safe for outpatient discharge. The ongoing regimen includes Cephalexin 500 mg PO every 6 hours for 10 days as prescribed. Prescription counseling was performed by nursing prior to release."
    },
    {
      "title": "PLAN & PRECAUTIONS",
      "text": "Resume normal daily activities as tolerated. Avoid strenuous exercise until cardiology follow-up in 1 to 2 weeks. Immediate emergency precautions detailed."
    }
  ],
